The four dials, their values and defaults, the stage order (plan, scope,
deps, lines, ask, the first denial winning), the presets, the /mixer grammar,
the glob matching, the manifest and install-command readers, the line
counting and the plan-mode read-only command allowlist are rewritten in Common
Lisp as one Nodecode cell: a hook on the organism's :tool point, the
operator's approval card for `ask`, and /mixer as a slash command. What the
rewrite does not carry: the Claude Code, Codex and Gemini CLI harness adapters
and their `agent-mixer` installer (this cell runs inside Nodecode, where there
is one tool and one hook); the desktop, dashboard and local-web consoles (the
/mixer command, the config section and the setup panel are the surface here);
the `extra_write_tools` setting (Nodecode has one tool, so no extra write
tools can be named); and the turn-start rules line that the original injects
into the model's context, since a Nodecode hook cannot add text to a request -
the board, the manual topic and every refusal carry the same words instead.
